## Summary
Canadian Minister Dominic LeBlanc indicated that Canada may introduce retaliatory tariffs on American goods effective August 25. The government is expected to make an announcement regarding this on Tuesday.

## Key Points
- Dominic LeBlanc, Canada's Minister of Internal Trade, suggested the imposition of retaliatory tariffs against the US.
- The tariffs are planned to take effect on August 25.
- This move is part of Canada's response in trade disputes with the United States.
- The official announcement is anticipated on Tuesday.


